                                      <TextRuns>
                                        <TextRun>
                                          <Value>8. RESERVATION OF OWNERSHIP RIGHTS: Weidmuller Electronics India shall have a general lien on all goods for the time being in possession and the property of the goods shall not pass to the Customer until completion of payment of all outstanding amounts, present or future arising out of the business relationship with the Customer, irrespective of legal arguments.

9.      INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS: Unless otherwise agreed in writing with Weidmuller, copyright exists in all documents supplied to the Customer or produced by Weidmuller under Customers instructions and is retained by Weidmuller. The contents of such documents or any part thereof shall not be disseminated in any form to any unauthorized person, institution, organization or company either directly or indirectly without the prior consent, of Weidmuller.  The Intellectual Property Rights in or relating to the products shall remain exclusively the property of Weidmuller and neither the Customer nor any agent or subcontractor or any other person authorized by the Customer shall, at any time, make use of same without prior written authorization.

10.     WARRANTY: Weidmuller warrants to the Customer that the products purchased shall be free from defects in material and workmanship. The warranty period for products is   6 (six) month after transfer of risk. The warranty does not cover, but not limited to, the following: : Unsuitable or unprofessional applications or storage, faulty installation by the Customer or third party, unauthorised attempts to rectify or modify natural wear and tear, incorrect or negligent treatment, chemical attack, electrical effects etc. upon which Weidmuller have no influence.  Any act, default or neglect on the part of the Customer and/or its employees, causing damages directly or indirectly. The warranty specified herein is in lieu of all other warranties, express or implied, Weidmüller hereby explicitly disclaims the implied warranties of merchantability and/or fitness for a purpose. 
The warranty provided is limited to the compliance with the technical specifications as stated in the respective data sheet of the product and/or quotation of Weidmüller, there is no warranties which extend beyond the description herein. In case of breach of warranty, as set forth above, Weidmuller shall at its sole discretion either rectify the product or supply a new product (corrective performance). The warranty period for the rectified object or the replaced part is 3 months. However, it runs at least to the expiry of the original warranty period. The warranty period for the product supplied is extended by the duration of the interruption of operations caused by the work of corrective performance.
Customer is obliged to notify any defect in products in writing, latest 8 days after receipt of products. If the complaints are justified, Weidmuller bear the cost of corrective performance otherwise, the customer should bear the costs.

11.     CLAIMS FOR COMPENSATION FOR DAMAGES: Save where expressly provided otherwise, all claims for damages and claims for reimbursement of expenses in respect of products supplied, including liabilities for indirect or consecutive damages such as but not limited to loss of profit, loss of production, economic loss, goodwill, anticipated savings, whether expressive or implied are excluded safe where, and in so far as, not admitted by mandatory provision of law, such as but not limited to wilful act or omission or any fundamental breach. 

12.     IMPOSSIBILITY, DELAY, CONTRACT AMENDMENT: Customer placing the order may withdraw from the contract if Weidmuller are not able to supply within the acknowledged delivery time. In case part deliveries, have taken place, only the remaining portion can be cancelled

13.     DISPUTES AND ARBITRATION: In respect of all matters / disputes arising out of, about or in relation to this Terms &amp; Condition or any relating contract as far as possible be mutually settled between the parties.  If this fails, dispute shall be resolved by the Sole Arbitrator appointed by mutual consent of both the parties in accordance with the provisions of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, and the Rules made thereunder, as amended from time to time.  The venue of such Arbitration shall be Bangalore and shall be conducted in English.  The Award of the Arbitrator / Arbitral Tribunal shall be final and binding on both the parties hereto.

14.     EXPORT CONTROL: Customer acknowledges that the conclusion of individual contracts and the respective performance of such shall be subject to national and international export control regulations. The sale and delivery may be subject to any applicable governmental approvals and Customer is obliged to provide declarations of end-use for the ordered goods in accordance with applicable export control regulations, upon request of Weidmuller. 

15.     CORPORATE RESPONSIBILITY: Customer will adhere to all applicable laws, including but not limited to anti-corruption laws.  Customer is aware that no form of extortion or bribery, including improper offers for payments or kickbacks, is tolerated. Customer obliges himself to comply with the Code of Conduct of Weidmuller which can be downloaded on the official Weidmuller homepage. Any breach of the obligations specified in the present provision will be treated as material breach which leads to immediate termination of business relationship without any further obligations of Weidmuller.

16.     PLACE OF JURISDICTION: The contractual obligations are governed by laws in India. The place of fulfilment of obligations shall be in Bangalore. The place of jurisdictions for all disputes shall be Bangalore and all suits by or against Weidmuller shall be filed in the Courts situated at Bangalore exclusively. 
</Value>
                                          <Style>
                                            <FontSize>5.7pt</FontSize>
                                            <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                                          </Style>
                                        </TextRun>
