                                      <TextRuns>
                                        <TextRun>
                                          <Value>1. GENERAL: All sales deliveries and services from and by Weidmuller Electronics India Pvt. Ltd (“Weidmuller”), shall be governed exclusively by the following terms and conditions and no deviation from these conditions, except those expressly accepted in writing by Weidmuller, shall be binding on Weidmuller. It is clearly understood that, by placing an order with Weidmuller, the Customer is deemed:
- To have accepted these Terms &amp; Conditions and
- To have waived off their conditions of purchase, if any, conflicting with these Terms &amp; Conditions. 

2.      QUOTATION AND CONCLUSION OF CONTRACT: The quotation is valid for a period of thirty days unless extended in writing. Weidmuller reserve the right to alter design and weight to be in conformity with the technical progress.
Mistakes that are due to printing, arithmetical and calculation which are apparent shall not give rise to any claim for compensation and shall not create any obligation. A Supply Contract will be concluded only upon Weidmullers written acknowledgement of Customers order. 

•       PRICE: Prices apply EXW (INCOTERMS 2010) Bangalore works or EXW (INCOTERMS 2010) Weidmuller warehouses. The prices do not include packing, taxes, other levies and freight Any other new taxes, levies, surcharge, cess etc. levied on the date of dispatch will be applicable and should be borne by the Customer. 
•       Price and terms are subject to change without notice. 
3.      The price ruling at the time of order acknowledgement will applycharges which are as follows: - 
3.1     Packing : 0.5% of basic price subject to a minimum of Rs.50/-
3.2     GST             : As Applicable at the time of delivery / Dispatch.
3.3     Freight : Freight to pay basis.
If Weidmuller is also responsible for assembly or erection and unless otherwise agreed, the Customer shall pay the agreed remuneration and any incidental costs required e. g. for travelling and transport as well as allowances as applicable.
•       .
4.      DESPATCH: Unless otherwise specified despatches shall be carried out uninsured and at the risk of the Customer. All deliveries shall be EXW (INCOTERMS 2010) Bangalore works or EXW (INCOTERMS 2010) Weidmuller Warehouse. If agreed between Customer and Weidmuller in writing despatches will be executed through road transport or by courier from Weidmuller’s authorised service provider. If specified by Customer on specific service providers, Weidmuller shall despatch the goods, however Weidmullers shall bear no responsibility for the quality of such service or for the transit damage and destruction during transit. Despatches by AIR can be made on request. All despatches are subject to availability of service of carriers. 

Customer shall intimate to Weidmuller in writing and supporting documents for any short supplies / wrong supplies within 3 days of goods receipt. Weidmuller shall not entertain claims post this period.

Government Modalities: Road Permits / Way Bill:  Customer shall revert in time for road permit / way bill to enable deliver of materials on time.  Weidmuller shall not reverse any Invoice related to delay or road permits not being provided by Customer.

5.      DELIVERY TIME AND FORCE MAJEURE: Weidmuller shall endeavour to keep the scheduled delivery dates. The delivery period commences with the acknowledgement of the order by Weidmuller. This however applies from that point of time, when all the technical and commercial details of the sales have been clarified and agreed between the Parties. 
For non-standard products, the delivery time will be informed with the order acknowledgement. Unless otherwise specified by the Customer, part delivery should be accepted by the Customer. Under no circumstances Weidmuller can accept penalties of any nature in case of delayed supply.
Unforeseen events (“Force Majeure Events”), whether in our Works or in any third-party undertakings, on which the manufacture and transportation of the object of supply materially depend and for which Weidmuller have been seen objectively, are not culpably responsible, release Weidmuller from the obligation to adhere to the delivery dates and such delivery dates will be updated shortly. These unforeseen events include, but are not limited to, natural calamities, labour disputes, wars and uprisings, strikes, action by public authorities, act of God and Traffic bottlenecks, dearth of raw materials and energy as well as major damage sustained through the action of water, fire. . In all such cases Weidmuller will inform Customer promptly of the delay. 

6.      PAYMENTS: Unless agreed otherwise in writing, payment shall be made by way of electronic payment (RTGS/ NEFT), Cheque, Demand Draft payable at Bangalore as per agreed payment terms or against Proforma invoice. Weidmuller shall bear its own bank charges.
For document through bank transactions, the amount invoiced has to be paid within 10 days after the documents have been presented by the Bank. Beyond this term interest @24% per annum will be charged if the invoice is not paid within 10 days of despatch.
It is not permitted to hold back payments or to make deductions because of possible counter claims. Interest at 24% per annum is payable on overdue payment outstanding. No “Stop payment” instruction to banks can be made after issue of cheque.
GST concession forms should be provided within __ period from the date of invoice. In case of non-receipt of GST Concession forms, Weidmuller shall raise the debit note for the differential tax amount. Weidmuller shall charge full tax for subsequent orders.

7.      RISK TRANSFER:  Risk is transferred to Customer upon despatch, in part or full, from Weidmuller factory in Bangalore or from Weidmuller warehouses in accordance with agreed INCOTERM 2010, EXW. Even where delivery has been agreed freight free, the risk shall pass to the Customer as follows: If the delivery does not include assembly or erection, at the time when it is shipped or picked up by the carrier. Upon the Customer's request, Weidmuller shall insure the delivery against the usual risks of transport at the Customer's expense.</Value>
                                          <Style>
                                            <FontSize>5.7pt</FontSize>
                                            <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                                          </Style>
                                        </TextRun>
                                      </TextRuns>
